Make @mbedtls_src's @arduino_esp32//:sdk_hdrs dependency PRIVATE
(implementation_deps, not deps).

mbedtls_src is built from source and its port .c files need the ESP-IDF SDK
headers (esp_*, soc, hal, lwip, freertos) — but its CONSUMERS do not need those
propagated: the player app / netstack already carry their own chip's full SDK
include set via //libs/board:arduino_core (-> @arduino_esp32//:core[_esp32c3]).
As `deps`, mbedtls re-propagated the esp32c6 SDK's ~315 `-I` dirs to every
consumer; on the esp32c3 build that stacked ON TOP of the c3 SDK's ~315 dirs and
overflowed the riscv32-esp-elf-g++ -> cc1plus exec ("posix_spawn: Argument list
too long"). implementation_deps compiles mbedtls against sdk_hdrs without leaking
those include dirs downstream, so each firmware build carries only its own chip's
SDK include set. Stable in Bazel 7. ABI/behaviour unchanged (same sources, same
compile flags); only the propagated compilation context shrinks.
diff --git a/nix/mbedtls_src.BUILD b/nix/mbedtls_src.BUILD
index c84e62a..5a03fe1 100644
--- a/nix/mbedtls_src.BUILD
+++ b/nix/mbedtls_src.BUILD
@@ -164,8 +164,13 @@ cc_library(
     copts = _MBEDTLS_COPTS,
     # Our symbols must satisfy the precompiled esp-tls/https_server callers.
     alwayslink = True,
-    # esp_* / soc / hal / lwip / freertos headers the port pulls in.
-    deps = ["@arduino_esp32//:sdk_hdrs"],
+    # esp_* / soc / hal / lwip / freertos headers the port pulls in — PRIVATE so
+    # the (esp32c6) SDK's ~315 -I dirs are used to compile mbedtls's own sources
+    # but are NOT re-propagated to consumers. Consumers (the player app / netstack)
+    # already carry their own chip's SDK include set via //libs/board:arduino_core;
+    # propagating the c6 set on top overflowed the g++ -> cc1plus argv on the c3
+    # build (c6 + c3 include lists). implementation_deps keeps mbedtls chip-neutral.
+    implementation_deps = ["@arduino_esp32//:sdk_hdrs"],
 )
 
